Verse 1:
[Dm]Watchman, tell us of [A7]the [Dm]night
[Dm]What [A]its [Dm]signs [A7]of [Dm]promise [A]are.
[Dm]Traveler, o’er yon moun[A7]tain’s [Dm]height,
[A]See [Dm]that [F]glo[Em]ry [Dm]beam[A7]ing [Dm]star.
[Bb]Watch[F]man, [Bb]does [Em]its [F]beau[C7]teous [F]ray
[Dm]Aught [A]of [Dm]joy [C]or [F]hope [E7]fore[Am]tell?
[Bb]Traveler, [F]yes; it [Dm]brings [Gm]the [A]day,
[Dm]Promised day of Is[A7]ra[Dm]el.

Verse 2:
[Dm]Watchman, tell us [A7]of the night, higher [Dm]yet that star ascends.
[Dm]Traveler, [A]blessedness and [Dm]light, peace [A7]and [Dm]truth its [A]course portends.
[Dm]Watchman, will its beams [A7]alone gild the spot [Dm]that gave them birth?
[A]Traveler, [Dm]ages are [F]its own; [Em]See [Dm]it bursts [A7]o'er all [Dm]the earth.

Verse 3:
[Dm]Watchman, tell us of [A7]the night, for the [Dm]morning seems to dawn.
[Dm]Traveler, [A]darkness takes [Dm]its flight, [A7]doubt [Dm]and terror [A]are withdrawn.
[Dm]Watchman, let your [A7]wanderings cease; hasten [Dm]to your quiet home.
[A]Traveler, [Dm]lo, the [F]Prince of [Em]Peace, lo, [Dm]the Son [A7]of God [Dm]is come!
